Independent review (skin-library-followups M1, WS-01): WS-01 (one commit, 2e2643b, v2.92.0) is mostly sound. It covers the five rule-changing rulings and nothing more: R-10 renames the tab to Skin, R-2 retires the stock look and keeps Ignore settings panel on by default, R-5 says custom widgets obey the Scope and defines the Scope as D-01/D-02 do, R-1 extends Ignore fonts to the HUD, and R-4 gives each skin its own HUD face. The other rulings (R-3, R-6..R-9, R-11, R-12) are correctly recorded in open-evolutions as library fixes with no rule to change. The version stamps agree: v2.92.0 / 2026-10-30 in STANDARDS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md and NEW_ADDON_CONTEXT.md, and the v2.91.0 entry moved to CHANGELOG.md. scripts/check-standard.sh passes: 2142 citations resolve, anti-patterns #1-#108 are contiguous, and the stamps are restated in all four places. The anti-pattern #107 addition, AUDIT Check skinning (c)/(d)/(g) and NEW_ADDON_CONTEXT (rule 24b, the #107 bullet, the definition-of-done line) agree with each other. The tab label, the Scope defaults (hosts already store ignorePanel=true), the HUD faces, PageButton/opts.stock and the PGFE register-row retirement all match what LibKa0s v1.81.0 ships. Problems found: one major factual mismatch with the library's HUD Ignore-fonts contract (S.Token answers nil, not the stored setting, and the host's nil fallback is unstated); two leftover 'Appearance tab' mentions; two overstatements in skinning-§3/§4 (Ignore fonts reaching 'every string', and the 'two exceptions' to Ka0s Default being unchanged); and a few nits in the wording of the audit check and widget constructors.
Findings: [major] WowAddonStandards standards/standards/skinning.md §6, bullet '*Ignore fonts* covers the HUD' (also STANDARDS.md v2.92.0 entry, paragraph (4)): The rule says that while fonts are ignored, `S.Resolve` and `S.Token` both 'answer the HUD element's own stored font setting for `hud.font` and `hud.outline`'. LibKa0s v1.81.0 does something else (CHANGELOG 'Ignore fonts reaches the HUD' and 'What a consumer owes' LK-01; DECISIONS D-09). Only `Resolve` answers the stored value, and gives nil for a stored FROM_SKIN. `Token('hud.font')` and `Token('hud.outline')` answer nil, and `BarStyle()`'s font/fontKey/outline are nil too. A host that passes any of these to SetFont or LSM:Fetch has to fall back on nil to its own stored pick, else its default. The standard never states that fallback. An addon that follows the rule literally can read Token expecting a face and pass nil to SetFont. AUDIT (g) and anti-pattern #107 ('a HUD face resolved around `S.Resolve`') also leave out the nil-fallback obligation. | [minor] WowAddonStandards standards/standards/skinning.md:80 (§5, 'The gate') and standards/standards/options-ui.md:343: R-10's rename is incomplete. skinning-§5 still says 'the Appearance tab says which condition failed', and options-ui:343 still says 'so is the Appearance tab of an addon that has adopted skins'. The diff renamed every other label mention to Skin, and the index entry claims the ripple is done. | [minor] WowAddonStandards standards/standards/skinning.md §3, '*Ignore fonts* reaches every string the library paints for the owner, windows and the HUD included' (also STANDARDS.md (3) and EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY 'keeps every string's own face'): This overstates what v1.81.0 does. The first-run picker's skin rows keep previewing each skin's own face whatever Ignore fonts says. That is decision D-15, and LibKa0s OptionsSkinPicker.lua:75 says 'names keep their own skins' faces: no font primitive reaches them' (it calls SetFont directly at :583). An auditor or tester reading 'every string' would report this designed behaviour as a bug. | [minor] WowAddonStandards standards/standards/skinning.md §4, 'Ka0s Default reproduces the Ka0s look as it was' (and STANDARDS.md (2), 'the two places Ka0s Default changes by ruling'): The bullet promises that 'every golden and color pin it carried stays green unchanged' with only two exceptions: retired stock windows, and first-skinned widgets taking 'Ka0s Default's face and tooltip palette'. v1.81.0 moves more Ka0s Default values than that. (a) R-8 changes `q.*` from rounded values to the client's exact values, and the library's own consumer note says pins of the rounded values move (LootHistory tests/test_skin_table.lua). (b) First-skinned widgets also change colours that are neither face nor tooltip: the drawer chevron becomes `icon.arrow` gold where the client's yellow art was, suggestion rows become `menu.text` 0.9 where they were white, and the id gray becomes `text.disabled`. So the promise as written is false for adopters. | [nit] WowAddonStandards standards/standards/skinning.md §1, 'Every custom library widget...' bullet: 'the `panel` flag every owned Widgets constructor takes': Not every Widgets constructor takes `panel`. WidgetsCopyWindow has no `opts.panel` in v1.81.0, and D-02 names only Dropdown, SearchBox, TestStrip, Autocomplete, LineChart and DragHandle, with ReorderList opting out instead. | [nit] WowAddonStandards AUDIT.md Check skinning (c), the new v1.81.0 sentence: The sentence requires that 'every library widget the addon places on a settings page passes `panel = true` (`S.Text`, the Widgets constructors)', but the reorder list is panel-scoped by default (skinning-§1). Read literally, an auditor would report a ReorderList that relies on its default. Separately, the check 'grep ... stockDefault returns nothing' also matches a comment that names the retired key. | [nit] WowAddonStandards standards/standards/open-evolutions.md, 'The skinning rollout's library follow-ups' entry: '`v1.81.0`, not yet tagged': LibKa0s v1.81.0 is already tagged locally at aefeba9 (LK-90) and is unpushed until finalize. 'Not yet tagged' will mislead a reader who checks the tag list.
